  "worked_solution": "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $100,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.09v-0.04w=0.05 & |\\times 100 \\\\ 0.02v-0.01w=0.2 & |\\times 100\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}9v-4w=5 \\\\ 2v-w=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $-4,$ we will get a $4w$ term that can cancel with the $-4w$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9v-4w=5 &  \\\\ 2v-w=20 & |\\,\\times (-4)\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}9v-4w=5 \\\\ -8v+4w=-80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $w$-variable and allows us to solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9v-\\cancel{4w} & =5 \\\\ -8v+\\cancel{4w} & =-80 \\\\ (9v-8v) & =(5-80) \\\\ v & =-75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $v=-75$ into the equation $2v-w=20$ to solve for $w:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v-w & =20 \\\\ 2(-75)-w & =20 \\\\ -150-w & =20 \\\\ -w & =170 \\\\ w & =-170\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $v=-75,\\,w=-170.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
